<Base title="About the workshop"><section class="page-intro container"><p class="eyebrow muted">ABOUT / WHY THIS EXISTS</p><h1>A place to<br/><em>follow the question<span class="dot">.</span></em></h1><p>VibeSource is an independent personal workshop for curiosity-driven engineering.</p></section><section class="container about-layout"><div class="about-main"><h2>Built from curiosity.</h2><p>Some ideas begin with a problem that needs solving. Others start with a simple question: what would happen if I tried this?</p><p>Here you'll find software, local AI experiments, connected devices, practical tools, and projects that occasionally wander away from their original plans.</p><p>This isn't a product catalogue or a collection of finished research papers. It's a working bench. Some projects are useful, some unfinished, and some exist simply because exploring them was interesting.</p><p>My background is in software engineering, but the workshop isn't limited to any particular technology or discipline. Curiosity gets to choose the next project.</p></div><aside class="about-aside"><span class="mini-label">WORKSHOP PRINCIPLES</span><div>01 <strong>Build to learn.</strong></div><div>02 <strong>Share the process.</strong></div><div>03 <strong>Stay curious.</strong></div><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/vibesource">Find me on GitHub ↗</a></aside></section></Base>
